<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul bus workers postpone Saturday's strike.</title>
<headline>Seoul bus workers postpone Saturday's strike.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seoul bus workers will put off a strike threatened for Saturday because of problems coordinating the action among 88 transport unions, a union statement said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Bus unions are affiliated with the Federation of Korean Trade Unions, whose chairman said earlier that bus services in Seoul and five other cities would be halted on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are postponing this action due to internal preparation problems such as coordinating action among the 88 Seoul city bus unions,&quot; the union statement said.</p>
<p>It was not clear whether other bus unions would go ahead with their action.</p>
</text>
